=========================================
Appendix B — ChannelsDVR Capability Dictionary
=========================================
This appendix defines the complete, authoritative capability dictionary for ChannelsDVR, mirroring the structure and rigor of Appendix A (SageTV).
It is designed explicitly for GitHub Copilot to generate:
* The ChannelsDVR MCP server
* The orchestrator routing logic
* The HTML5 remote integration
* The Unified Session Manager’s session resolution logic
* The LLM’s structured intent mapping
ChannelsDVR is treated as a firstclass system, equal to SageTV.

B.1 Overview
ChannelsDVR exposes a modern, JSONbased HTTP API with:
* Playback control
* Recording scheduling
* Commercial skip
* EPG search
* Client enumeration
* Job status
* Storage usage
* Metadata queries
This capability dictionary defines:
1. Entities
2. State
3. Actions
4. Resources
5. Tools
6. Safety levels
7. Session model
8. Playback context model
This is the only surface the LLM is allowed to use for ChannelsDVR.

B.2 Entity Model
B.2.1 Media Entities
EntityDescriptionFieldsRecordingA completed DVR recordingid, title, episode, season, channel, start_time, end_time, file_path, commercial_markersScheduledRecordingA future scheduled recordingid, title, channel, start_time, end_timeProgramEPG program metadataid, title, description, actors, year, ratingChannelA TV channelid, number, name, HD, lineupJobA DVR job (recording, commercial detection, transcoding)id, type, status, progress
