B.7 Session Resolution Model
The Unified Session Manager resolves the active playback session by:
1. Querying ChannelsDVR MCP for active sessions (/sessions)
2. Matching device_id to client_id
3. Returning: 
o session_id
o media_id
o position
o duration
o state
This ensures commands always target the correct playback session.

B.8 Playback Context Model
The LLM receives a structured context block:
{
  "device_id": "livingroom-shield",
  "session_id": "channels-123",
  "media": {
    "id": "rec-98765",
    "title": "The Office",
    "episode": "S03E14",
    "position": 1420,
    "duration": 1800,
    "state": "playing",
    "commercial_markers": [120, 480, 900, 1320]
  }
}
This allows the LLM to:
* Interpret commands
* Resolve ambiguity
* Provide natural responses
* Trigger commercial skip correctly

